            "text": "{\"description\":\"The main stone surface shows a rough relief carving with several recessed shapes and raised outlines. Near the center is a figure-like form with a pointed or beak-like head area, a rounded body, and incised vertical marks below; on both sides are additional worn circular and curved carvings.\",\"avian\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"A central carved figure has a pointed, beak-like head/projection and a body-like form, making it visually birdlike on the visible surface.\",\"box\":[0.38,0.12,0.67,0.78]},\"large_face\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"There are circular depressions and curved cuts that could suggest facial parts, especially left of center, but no clear large human face with definite facial features is visible.\",\"box\":null},\"scorpion\":{\"answer\":\"uncertain\",\"evidence\":\"Some curved and segmented-looking incisions appear on the right and lower central areas, but legs and an upturned segmented tail are not clear enough to identify as a scorpion.\",\"box\":null},\"round_motif\":{\"answer\":\"present\",\"evidence\":\"Distinct circular recessed motifs are visible, including one near the lower-left/central area that is not clearly an eye, nostril, or navel.\",\"box\":[0.36,0.55,0.45,0.67]},\"three_arches\":{\"answer\":\"absent\",\"evidence\":\"I do not see three repeated arch-topped forms arranged side by side in a row on the visible carved surface.\",\"box\":null},\"limitations\":\"The stone is heavily worn and pitted, the photograph is monochrome and low contrast, and parts of the carving are obscured by shadow and foreground stone, making some shapes ambiguous.\"}",
